-- **Editorial marketing layer**: the public marketing surface (unauthenticated `/`, `use-cases/*`, `compare/*`, `alternatives/*`, `features/*`, `tools/*`, `pricing`, `trust`, `demo`, `shared/[token]`, `document-diff`) uses the scoped editorial system in `frontend/src/app/editorial.css` — every rule under `.dt-editorial`. **Light AND dark are both required** (HIG: every custom colour needs both): `.dt-editorial` is warm paper (`--ed-paper` `#eae8e3`, `--ed-ink` `#20211e`, `--ed-signal` terracotta `#843c28`), `.dark .dt-editorial` a warm near-black that is NOT an inversion and NOT zinc (`--ed-paper` `#171614`, `--ed-ink` `#ece9e2`, `--ed-signal` `#e0957a`). Olive = verified only; amber `--ed-evidence` = citation only. **Dark tokens must reuse the `--ed-*` names** — ~40 components write `var(--ed-paper-2)` inline and the `!important` counter-rule resolves `var(--ed-paper)`, so new names would leave them light-on-dark. Never hardcode `#fff`/`white` on an `--ed-*` background; use `var(--ed-paper)` so it inverts. Type: **Fraunces 600 for marketing `h1`/`h2` only** (optical size follows the rendered size — do NOT pin `"opsz" 144`, it crowds words together at phone sizes); IBM Plex Sans for every other glyph; no italic `<em>` in headlines, no mono labels, no ALL-CAPS eyebrows. Structure follows Apple's grammar: one claim → one sentence → **exactly one filled `.ed-cta` per view** → the product; secondary actions use `.ed-cta-quiet` or `.ed-link`. Liquid Glass (`.ed-glass`) is permitted ONLY in the functional layer (the sticky header and popovers) — never on cards, FAQ rows, banners, tables or hero art. **Design decision 2026-09-20 (supersedes 2026-05-20):** the warm-paper terracotta identity is kept (re-affirmed by the owner, who chose it over a neutral rebrand), but the light-only rule, content-layer glass, 3px buttons and the two-surface split are retired; the app joins the paper system in Phases 3–4. Do not re-propose a neutral/blue rebrand, and do not reintroduce a second surface treatment. Plan: `.collab/plans/2026-09-20-apple-design-direction.md`. Marketing pages compose the shared editorial kit in `frontend/src/components/marketing/` (`MarketingShell`, `EditorialMarketingHeader`, `EdPageHero` — `variant="product"` for the product-first hero, `EdSection`, `EdProse`, `EdFeatureList`, `EdCardGrid`, `EdStepRow`, `EdFaqList`, `EdCtaBanner`, `EdComparisonTable`, `EdInlineCell`, `EdRelatedLinks`, `EdCheckList`, `EdChoiceList`) — `MarketingShell` supplies the `.dt-editorial` root, so kit components never add it themselves. Keep editorial styles scoped under `.dt-editorial`, including reduced-motion rules; do not let them leak into the functional app UI (`editorial.css` is imported globally, so an unscoped selector hits every app route). Do not apply the zinc/blue rule to editorial components. Two dual-surface components are sanctioned: `DocumentDiffPanel` takes `surface="app"|"editorial"`; the global `CookieConsentBanner` detects the surface itself. Pages still on the zinc/blue app palette: `about`, `contact`, `imprint`, `privacy`, `terms`, `blog/*`. **Never touch one half of the `!important` pair alone**: `globals.css` `.dt-stitch-root > .min-h-screen { background: transparent !important }` and its `editorial.css` counter-rule `.dt-stitch-root > .dt-editorial` — removing either blanks the paper on every marketing page.
